    "en": {
      "representative_place": "Horský park – historic woodland park on the north-western edge of the Old Town",
      "facts": [
        {
          "id": "fact_001",
          "title": "Horský park: the city woodland that grew from the old Študentský les",
          "text": "Horský park was created in the second half of the 19th century by shaping an existing woodland known as Študentský les, or Student Forest. Bratislava mayor Henrich von Justi played an important role in its creation and supported the Bratislava Beautification Society. The widening of Hlboká cesta around 1870 opened up the slopes and made recreational use of the new park possible. The Justi Memorial became its natural focal point; the city erected it in 1909, and it was made by sculptor Alojz Rigele. The park has retained its woodland character, with native trees and species planted later. Today it is also a protected area of ecological, landscape and recreational importance. Its management must balance the protection of old woodland with the safety of visitors."
